## 🔧 Robustness Improvements

| # | Improvement | Priority | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Fix interval skipping** (Bug 1) | 🔴 High | 1 line |
| 2 | **Add stale-odds guard** in rechecker | 🔴 High | 5 lines |
| 3 | **Log total pending count** each rechecker cycle | 🟡 Medium | 1 line |
| 4 | **Add `__init__.py`** to paper_trading package | 🟢 Low | 1 file |
| 5 | **Cap [_trades](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/paper_trading/paper_trade_recorder.py#47-51) list growth** with a max size or ring buffer | 🟡 Medium | 10 lines |
| 6 | **Add rechecker metrics**: total rechecks, avg recheck latency | 🟡 Medium | 15 lines |
| 7 | **Log which specific leg was suspended** in break detail | 🟢 Low | 3 lines |

### On item 5 — unbounded memory growth:

The [_trades](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/paper_trading/paper_trade_recorder.py#47-51) list in [PaperTradeRecorder](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/paper_trading/paper_trade_recorder.py#27-145) grows forever. Over a 24-hour session with 100+ alerts, this is fine. Over a multi-day run, it's a slow memory leak. Consider either:
- A max size with FIFO eviction
- Periodic flush to disk/DB after trades reach terminal state

---

## ✅ What's Done Well

- **Exact matching** is strict and correct — operator, selection, market, period, line all matched
- **`frozen_arb`** is a full `model_dump` snapshot that's never mutated — clean audit trail
- **Break reasons** are stored as both enum and human string — good for both code and logs
- **Reporter metrics** cover all the right dimensions (survival rates, decay, operator pairs)
- **3-way market support** is properly handled throughout
- **Event-level grouping** in the rechecker minimizes Redis round-trips
